[Music]  is this the moment of truth when  historians come back to look at  Britain's relationship with Europe is it  now they'll talk about or will they  focus on something else will it be the  leave vote in 2016  David Cameron's Bloomberg speech a few  years earlier well what if the events  were living through were really set in  train when we were looking the other way  when our eyes were glued to the Olympics  and we celebrated the Diamond Jubilee  what if the seminal year the moment our  fate became preordained was 2012 we  didn't notice it at the time but a chain  reaction was happening beneath our feet  causing ripple effects that were still  feeling now this is the story about how  seemingly unconnected events in Europe  Africa the Middle East and most of all  here in Britain have left us where we  are today it is the story about how 2012  was the year everything changed  it might seem an odd yes choose in some  sense this 2012 was the year of Europe's  greatest triumph awarded the Nobel Peace  Prize faded as the world's most advanced  civilized continent and you can  understand why it's the ultimate story  of turning defeat into victory it's  impossible to tell Europe's story  without considering this the aftermath  of the second world war a continent in  ruins and a question how to make  conflict like this a history in 1946  Churchill gave a famous speech where he  called for the creation of the United  States of Europe no longer would the  continent be locked in conflict it would  be locked in political union but ever  since then we've been asking ourselves a  question what about us are we in the  club or out of it  for much of that time the answer was  focused on the economic relationships  steer clear of the politics but every  five years came a new European treaty  adding more EU power increasing  integration creating a closer and closer  Union and when was the next treaty jus  20  twelve but then events intervened the  euro crisis in Spain island and 